      "side": 1,
      "message": "Two lifecycle notes here:\n1. `disconnectedCallback()` removes `--sidebar-wrapper-top`, but `connectedCallback()` does not recompute it. If the element is disconnected and reconnected while `hideSide` is `false` (e.g., when reparented in the DOM), `firstUpdated()` will not run again and `updated()` will not see `hideSide` change, leaving `--sidebar-wrapper-top` unset until a scroll/resize event. Calling `if (this.hasUpdated) this.updateSidebarTop();` in `connectedCallback()` avoids this.\n2. `firstUpdated()` calling `this.updateSidebarTop()` is redundant with `updated()`, since Lit includes `hideSide` in `changedProperties` on the initial update and calls `updated()` immediately after `firstUpdated()`. (Also minor: `!this.sidebarWrapper` in the guard on line 82 is no longer needed now that `getBoundingClientRect()` is called on `this`.)\n\n_— from potto_",
