      "writtenOn": "2026-10-15T22:43:11Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "In `gr-change-view` and `gr-diff-view`, `--change-header-height` and `--diff-header-height` start at `0px` (in `app-theme.ts` and after `disconnectedCallback()`) and are updated asynchronously via `ResizeObserver`. Because `updateSidebarTop()` runs synchronously in `firstUpdated()`/`updated()` before the parent view\u0027s `ResizeObserver` fires, `this.topReference.getBoundingClientRect().top` initially evaluates with a `0px` header height while `this.getBoundingClientRect().top` already includes the header\u0027s DOM height—causing `--sidebar-wrapper-top` to be set even when no banner is present.\n\nIf the sticky header subsequently grows (e.g., when async status chips, actions, or diff subheader items render while the sidebar is open) or if a plugin banner (`\u003cgr-endpoint-decorator name\u003d\"banner\"\u003e`) is injected or dismissed asynchronously without a `window` `scroll`/`resize` event, `updateSidebarTop()` is not re-run. Because `.sidebar-wrapper` uses `top: var(--sidebar-wrapper-top, var(--sidebar-top, 0px))` (line 118), a stale `--sidebar-wrapper-top` overrides `--sidebar-top`, either overlapping the expanded header or leaving a gap after banner dismissal until the user scrolls.\n\nConsider:\n1. Using `top: max(var(--sidebar-wrapper-top, 0px), var(--sidebar-top, 0px));` on `.sidebar-wrapper` (line 118) so a stale `--sidebar-wrapper-top` can never pull the sidebar above `var(--sidebar-top, 0px)` when `--sidebar-top` increases.\n2. Observing layout shifts (e.g., via a `ResizeObserver` on `document.documentElement` / `document.body`) so `updateSidebarTop()` runs when header or banner heights change dynamically without a window scroll/resize.\n\n_— from potto_",
